# boot/kaem/build-*.kaem is generated from the Makefile's own source file
# list (tools/gen-kaem.sh, `make kaem`) -- a three-way text merge of it is
# never the right resolution, since two branches that each add a source
# file conflict here textually even though the "right" merge is just
# regenerating from the merged tree. Route both files through the
# ntlibc-kaem merge driver (tools/merge-kaem.sh) instead of git's default
# text merge, during `merge`, `rebase` and `cherry-pick` alike.
#
# The driver command itself is per-clone config (git does not read
# merge.*.driver from the repository) -- see ./configure, which sets it up
# the same way it sets core.hooksPath for .githooks, and CONTRIBUTING.md's
# "Merging/rebasing/cherry-picking across a source-file add" section for
# how it actually resolves a conflict and the manual fallback.
boot/kaem/build-i386.kaem merge=ntlibc-kaem
boot/kaem/build-x86_64.kaem merge=ntlibc-kaem

# test/*.generated.md are the two gap reports (tools/posix-gapmap.sh,
# tools/libc-test-map.sh), and they are almost entirely DERIVED: a greedy
# header closure, a per-directory ledger, a reconciliation, a dozen
# counts in prose. Land a header on one branch and a different one on
# another and every number in both files moves, so a three-way TEXT merge
# of them is not merely conflict-prone, it is meaningless -- the right
# answer is neither side's text.
#
# Unlike boot/kaem/, though, these two have a separable data layer: each
# report carries the rows it was rendered from in an HTML comment at its
# end. tools/merge-gendata.sh merges THOSE, key by key, and re-renders --
# a real resolution rather than a text reconciliation, and still a pure
# function of the three blobs git hands a merge driver, which is the one
# thing merge-kaem.sh's header shows a driver can rely on mid-merge.
#
# Same per-clone config story as ntlibc-kaem above -- see ./configure and
# CONTRIBUTING.md's "Merging a generated report" section.
test/POSIX-GAP-MAP.generated.md merge=ntlibc-gendata
test/LIBC-TEST-MAP.generated.md merge=ntlibc-gendata
